(2765, 'sharp', '/ʃɑːrp/', 'adverb, adjective, noun', '{"zh-TW":["【主要意義-形容詞】鋒利的；尖銳的","【次要意義-副詞】準時地；整點（時間）","【次要意義-形容詞】聰明的；機靈的","【次要意義-形容詞】突然的；急劇的"],"en":["[primary - adjective] having a fine cutting edge or point","[secondary - adverb] exactly at the stated time","[secondary - adjective] intelligent and quick to learn","[secondary - adjective] sudden and intense"]}', NULL, 'at 9 o''clock sharp / sharp decline / sharp contrast / a sharp eye', '[{"en":"The meeting begins at 8 o clock sharp; latecomers will not be admitted.","zh-TW":"會議於8點整開始，遲到者不予入場。"},{"en":"There was a sharp decline in sales during the fourth quarter.","zh-TW":"第四季度的銷售額出現了急劇下降。"},{"en":"She has a sharp eye for detail that makes her an excellent proofreader.","zh-TW":"她對細節的敏銳眼光使她成為一名出色的校對員。"}]', '{"adverb":"sharply","noun":"sharpness"}', 'sharp 作副詞表「準時地/整點」（at 9 sharp），是 TOEIC 會議通知常見用法；sharp decline/increase 表「急劇的下降/上升」，也是財務報告高頻搭配。', 2, 2765, NULL),
